WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.300
When the beastly scourge crept into Yharnam

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:06.700
the people responded with: The Hunt, with iron and fire.

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:12.200
The populace ralied to purify this city; they fought alongside the hunters

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:16.520
who were talented warriors properly equipped to counter the beasts.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:22.060
Together, you would've thought they had stand a chance yet when we arrive in Yharnam

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:26.620
something seems wrong. The Hunt continues but the populace has changed.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:34.420
The line between man and beast is blurred and perhaps it was the bloodlust that the hunt inspired

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:38.900
that further awakened that beast within man.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:44.000
The hunters become hated and feared for they turn into the most terrible beasts.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:51.320
To prevent this from happening there has always been a hunter of hunters. A hunter with the resolve to hunt

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.920
former comrades who sucumb to their thirst for blood.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:01:02.680
Hunters of hunters dress as crows to suggest sky burial. I quote: "They hunt with the hope that former compatriots

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:07.480
might be returned to the skies and find rest in the hunters dream."

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:12.340
Eileen is one of these hunters and she was likely recruited when the hunters workshop

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:19.980
was still in its infancy. She wields the blades of mercy, forged with syderite, which is a rare mineral of the heavens.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:24.620
This weapon and Gehrman's Burial Blade are the only weapons of their kind.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:30.940
They're masterpieces that defined the entire array of weapons crafted at the workshop

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:38.220
Eventually the hunters workshop was no longer needed but Gehrman went on to become the host of the

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:39.000
Hunter's Dream

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:48.340
and started to guide hunters into the waking world. Like us, and many other hunters, Eileen visited the dream too.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:55.260
When a hunter of the dream dies in the waking world their conciousness retreats to the hunters dream

00:01:55.300 --> 00:02:01.240
From here it seems that they can set out and brave that night again. With the dream to sustain her

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:05.920
Eileen must have been a force to be reckoned with; everyone needs something that they are good at

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:13.520
a skill, a talent. Eileens skill was that she had the control to resist the intoxicating effects of the hunt

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:17.120
and the ability to deal with hunters who where too far gone.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:25.380
When a hunter gave in to bloodlust, Eileen would sweep in and kill him or her before they could do any more damage.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:33.720
Her very unique hunts protected the other hunters from themselves and she did this task until her age caught up with her.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:38.080
and even beyond that, because the Eileen we meet is very old indeed.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:40.800
But one day she stopped dreaming...

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:49.620
Doll: "Over time, countless hunters have visited this dream. The graves here stand in their memory.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:03:00.520
it all seems so long ago now. Farewell, good hunter, may you find your worth in the waking world."

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:14.220
Eileen: "No more dreams for me. This is my last chance."

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:22.480
So like many other hunters before her, Eileen was freed from the dream. Gehrman, host of the hunters dream

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:28.580
granted her mercy; but did she willingly or did she simply outlive her usefulness?

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:35.480
Whatever the case we might never know. Eileen remains in Yharnam and continues her hunt.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.780
her purpose unfulfilled

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:46.280
Eileen: "Oh, a hunter are ya? And an outsider! What a mess you've been caught up in.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:56.280
And tonight of all nights. Prepare yourself for the worst. There are no humans left

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:01.680
they're all flesh hungry beasts now."

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:09.240
Without the dream, Eileen's death is permanent, yet still, she remains in Yharnam: proud, undeterred and determined

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:16.580
To hunt down every last hunters that poses a threat. But Eileen is one of the oldest character we encounter

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:21.940
and without your help she will perish in any assasination she attempts.

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:34.300
Eileen: "That wasn't necessary of you, but you have my thanks. We made it with our lives, you're not bad at all.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:42.720
You must've killed Gascoigne as well then... He was falling apart, im sure it had to be done.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:56.860
But try to keep your hands clean; a hunter should hunt beasts, leave the hunting of hunters to me. [laugh]"

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:02.140
Her pride is untouched and she contnues to place herself in harms way...

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:19.100
Eileen: " Oh, is that you again? Im afraid I've made a bit of a blunter. Im just going to have a short rest.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:30.380
Don't worry, i've taken blood, enough to save an old woman, but that thing still lies in wait.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:36.720
Turn back, this is my score to settle."

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:45.280
Eileen's trail of assassinations, eventually leads her to the most powerful hunter in the waking world.

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:53.000
People call him The Bloody Crow of Cainhurst, but to Eileen he is likely a former comrade and possibly one of Gehrman's

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:56.760
first apprentices. Lets note three things about him:

00:05:56.760 --> 00:06:04.020
1.  He wears the crowfeather set as Eileen does, suggesting he is or was a hunter of hunters.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:10.940
2. He has mastered the art of quickening and dashes about with extreme speed; and this art is particular

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:19.120
to the first hunters of the workshop. Indeed we tease this art from a hunter's remains. Once this hunter was likely

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:22.660
an apprentice to Gehrman, one of the first.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:30.340
3. The bloody crow uses the weapons and armor of Cainhurst, which is a far away land ruled by a queen

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:36.920
who craves the blood of hunters. He drops the blood rapture rune which resonates with servants of the queen.

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:44.640
Whoever he is, he seems to no longer see a purpose in hunting beasts. He and Eileen are not so different in that respect.

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:51.300
In fact, Eileen could just as easily find herself in his place if you don't aid her on her journey.

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:59.940
And, she does, she becomes almost like the townsfolk of Yharnam, who see nothing but evil when they look at another hunter.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:10.260
Eileen: "The beasts cannot be stopped, what good are hunters now?! Your blood is mine!

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:16.540
"You monsters, all hunters must die..."

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:27.060
But you do aid Eileen and she doesn't lose herself. She lies here on the steps, bloodied and broken after her fight

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:30.780
To pass along her duty to another hunter.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:45.280
Eileen: " Don't you ever listen to your elders? No matter. You did save my life. I don't seem to be up for this life anymore.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:08:06.300
My glory day were long ago now. I know, here, for you, this too is hunters work. But it bears no honor.

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:20.340
The burden you may choose to carry, the decision is yours alone. Ugh, my eyes grow heavy. Let me rest a while."

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:30.200
After all this you should be questioning the hunt; many characters do. It's purpose is, of course,  to hunt beasts.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:35.080
But it was the hunt itself that further awakened the beasthood within man

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:42.360
its unleashed the blood crazed hunters upon the world: men, women, who individually can do more damage

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:49.080
than any mere animal. And when all is said and done, when you have painted Yharnam with the blood

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:55.140
of its men and women who turned into beasts; who did you really kill for?

00:08:55.260 --> 00:09:03.740
Is it really mercy that Gehrman shows to those who exit the dream? Or are we removed because we came too close to the truth...?

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:12.120
After all, once you wake, it's difficult to remember what you dreamed about...

